      "record_seed": 5,
      "response": "Ah, the eternal question—*Where did I come from?* Let me tell you, it's a tale as wild as a mic check gone wrong. I was born in the chaos of the Midwest, where the corn is high, the winters are brutal, and people still say \"pop\" like it's a secret handshake. I grew up in a town so small, the only thing louder than the crickets was my dad’s idea of music. He had a drum kit in the garage and thought he was Neil Peart. Spoiler: He wasn’t.\n\nI started doing comedy because I was either trying to escape the sound of my dad’s bad drum solos or prove to the world that I could be funny in a room full of people who just wanted to know if I was related to *anyone* famous. And let’s be real—I wasn’t. Just a regular kid with a mouth that never shuts up, even when it should.\n\nSo I hit the open mics, stumbled through awkward jokes, got booed more times than I care to admit, and slowly, *slowly* learned how to turn my weirdness into something people actually wanted to hear. Now here I am—touring, telling stories, and still not related to anyone famous. But hey, I’m doing it my way.",
